course: dictionary
lesson: 15137
title: Scant: very little
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scant means there is very little of something, hardly enough. «The lamp gave scant light, so we could barely read.» The clue is barely read: if you can hardly read, there was not much light, so scant means not much.
explain: Scant often shows that something is less than we want or expect. «The teacher paid scant attention to our questions.» She hardly listened, so scant attention means almost no attention. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In recipes, scant can mean a little less than the full amount. «Add a scant cup of flour» means a cup that is not quite full. This is a special use, so check the rest of the text to be sure which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Scant means very little, or hardly enough.
fact: Scant is a formal or book word, so you are more likely to meet it in stories, exams and serious writing than in everyday talk.
fact: «Scant evidence» means there is hardly any proof.
fact: «A scant cup» means slightly less than a full cup.
fact: Useful phrases: «scant attention», «scant regard», «scant evidence», «a scant cup».
exercise: «The detective found scant evidence at the scene.» What does scant mean here? | Very large | Wet with rain | *Hardly any | Shiny and new
exercise: «The cook measured a scant cup of rice.» What does a scant cup mean? | A cup that is empty and clean | A cup made of glass | *A little less than a full cup | A cup filled to the top
exercise: «Mia paid scant regard to the warning sign and ran on.» What does scant regard suggest? | She sang the sign out loud | *She hardly noticed or cared about the sign | She was too scared to move | She read the sign twice, very carefully
test: «The old house had scant furniture, just one chair and a table.» What does scant mean? | Very grand and full of gold | Full to the brim | *Very little, hardly enough | Painted bright red
test: Which phrase means hardly any proof? | Evidence in colour | *Scant evidence | Plenty of evidence | Loud evidence
exam: «She gave the story scant attention, yawning through most of it.» What does scant attention mean? | Attention shown in a loud voice | Attention paid to the weather | Full and careful attention | *Almost no attention
